# Line-ending conversion must never touch a document.
#
# Git guesses binary by looking for NUL bytes. A real PDF has compressed
# streams and so is guessed correctly, but a small uncompressed one is pure
# ASCII and gets treated as text — and tests/fixtures/encrypted-minimal.pdf is
# exactly that. Expanding its LFs to CRLFs on checkout shifts every byte offset
# in its xref table, so the file would arrive corrupt on a fresh clone and the
# test that depends on it would fail for reasons nobody would look for here.
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
